					"title": "Classic Pancakes",
					"source_url": "",
					"description": "Weekend pancakes made with pantry staples.",
					"image": "",
					"prep_time": "20 min",
					"servings": 4,
					"category": "Breakfast",
					"ingredients": "1 1/2 cups all-purpose flour\n3 1/2 tsp baking powder\n1 tbsp sugar\n1/4 tsp salt\n1 1/4 cups milk\n1 egg\n3 tbsp melted butter",
					"instructions": "Mix flour, baking powder, sugar, and salt in a large bowl.\nMake a well in the center and pour in milk, egg, and melted butter. Mix until smooth.\nHeat a griddle over medium-high heat and lightly oil.\nPour batter onto griddle, using about 1/4 cup per pancake.\nCook until bubbles form and edges are dry, then flip and cook until golden."
				},
